# Environment files — do not access

Never read, open, grep, or otherwise access `.env` or other local environment files that may contain API keys and secrets.

## Prohibited

- Using the Read tool on `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.development`, `.env.production`, or similar
- Running shell commands that read those files (e.g. `cat .env`, `type .env`, `Get-Content .env`, `grep` against `.env*`)
- Reproducing secret values in chat, commits, code, or edits

## Allowed

- Read `.env.example` for variable names and structure only (no real secrets)
- Ask the user to confirm values or set them locally themselves

If a task requires an env value, tell the user which variable to set — never read `.env` to obtain it.
